WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.367
-Welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.367 --> 00:00:04.634
This is it.
You're here.

00:00:04.634 --> 00:00:07.534
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you for watching.

00:00:07.534 --> 00:00:10.701
Well, guys, today is the
first day of February.

00:00:10.701 --> 00:00:12.334
That's right.
[ Cheers ]

00:00:12.334 --> 00:00:14.067
You can tell it's almost
Groundhog Day

00:00:14.067 --> 00:00:16.400
because Tom Brady
announced he's retiring again.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.601
[ Laughter ]

00:00:18.601 --> 00:00:20.267
That's right.
This morning, Tom Brady posted

00:00:20.267 --> 00:00:23.334
an emotional video announcing
his retirement from football.

00:00:23.334 --> 00:00:25.133
If you haven't seen it yet,
here it is.

00:00:25.133 --> 00:00:26.367
-Good morning, guys.

00:00:26.367 --> 00:00:29.033
I'll get to the point
right away.

00:00:29.033 --> 00:00:31.834
I'm retiring.
For good.

00:00:31.834 --> 00:00:33.200
-Oh.
That's nice.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.667
Don't worry.
Brady will be okay.

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:36.834
Based on the deserted landscape
behind him,

00:00:36.834 --> 00:00:39.868
I think he landed a role
on "The Last of Us."

00:00:39.868 --> 00:00:42.367
[ Laughter ]
That's what I think.

00:00:42.367 --> 00:00:44.801
Yeah, everyone got emotional
watching the heartfelt message.

00:00:44.801 --> 00:00:48.067
Even Bill Belichick's shirt
holes grew three sizes today.

00:00:48.067 --> 00:00:50.000
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:51.200
But what an amazing career.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:54.234
Brady played for 23 seasons.

00:00:54.234 --> 00:00:55.300
Yeah, he was around for --
[ Cheers ]

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:56.434
Yeah.
Amazing.

00:00:56.434 --> 00:01:00.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:00.567 --> 00:01:01.868
He was around for a long time.

00:01:01.868 --> 00:01:04.133
Let's just say Brady
was the only active NFL player

00:01:04.133 --> 00:01:06.467
to see "Top Gun" 1 and 2
in theaters.

00:01:06.467 --> 00:01:09.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.167 --> 00:01:11.434
Yep, Brady is done,
and in a related story,

00:01:11.434 --> 00:01:14.234
tickets to next year's
Buccaneers game are now free.

00:01:14.234 --> 00:01:16.601
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.601 --> 00:01:18.601
Some more big news today --
the FBI searched

00:01:18.601 --> 00:01:20.567
President Biden's beach house
in Delaware

00:01:20.567 --> 00:01:22.501
for classified documents.

00:01:22.501 --> 00:01:24.434
First, they searched near
Biden's corvette,

00:01:24.434 --> 00:01:26.667
now they're searching
his beach house.

00:01:26.667 --> 00:01:27.901
I'm starting to think
Biden created this whole scandal

00:01:27.901 --> 00:01:30.434
as a humblebrag.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.434 --> 00:01:32.367
"Why don't you check
by my infinity pool?"

00:01:32.367 --> 00:01:33.834
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.834 --> 00:01:35.868
"Maybe there's something behind
the Picasso, I don't know."

00:01:35.868 --> 00:01:38.501
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.501 --> 00:01:40.100
After the FBI
completed the search,

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.234
a White House spokesman
announced the results.

00:01:42.234 --> 00:01:44.834
-Today, in a planned,
consensual search

00:01:44.834 --> 00:01:46.200
with the Justice Department,
they went through

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:48.200
the Rehoboth beach house,

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:51.534
and no classified marked
documents were found.

00:01:51.534 --> 00:01:54.334
-Yeah. Apparently, Moby now
works for the White House.

00:01:54.334 --> 00:01:58.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.767 --> 00:02:01.334
They didn't find any documents
at Biden's beach house,

00:02:01.334 --> 00:02:03.801
but even more embarrassing,
they found a sign that said,

00:02:03.801 --> 00:02:05.000
"Where my beaches at?"

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.601
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.601 --> 00:02:08.334
-That's kinda weird.

00:02:08.334 --> 00:02:10.400
Speaking of Biden,
today the White House announced

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:14.434
that he will get his annual
physical on February 16th.

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:16.534
It's gonna be crazy
after Biden's colonoscopy

00:02:16.534 --> 00:02:18.167
when the doctor says,
"There's no easy way

00:02:18.167 --> 00:02:20.701
to tell you this, but we found
more classified documents."

00:02:20.701 --> 00:02:26.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.634 --> 00:02:28.767
Switching gears,
everyone's excited about this.

00:02:28.767 --> 00:02:32.734
Today, Beyoncé announced
the Renaissance World Tour.

00:02:32.734 --> 00:02:36.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:39.334
Fans are pumped,
while Ticketmaster is like,

00:02:39.334 --> 00:02:41.167
"F my L."

00:02:41.167 --> 00:02:43.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.267 --> 00:02:45.901
Beyoncé made the announcement
around 9:00 a.m.

00:02:45.901 --> 00:02:47.634
Yep, she basically gave
Tom Brady an hour

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:48.934
to trend on Twitter,
then, she was like,

00:02:48.934 --> 00:02:50.167
"This is mine now."

00:02:50.167 --> 00:02:51.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.634 --> 00:02:53.467
Some more entertainment news --
it was just announced that,

00:02:53.467 --> 00:02:56.434
after 21 seasons,
Dr. Phil's daytime talk show

00:02:56.434 --> 00:02:58.934
is coming to an end.

00:02:58.934 --> 00:03:01.067
You know this morning
Dr. Phil's publicist was like,

00:03:01.067 --> 00:03:03.501
"It'll definitely be the biggest
retirement news of the day."

00:03:03.501 --> 00:03:07.267
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.267 --> 00:03:09.167
"F my L."

00:03:09.167 --> 00:03:10.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.601 --> 00:03:12.601
Yeah, today, Dr. Phil released
a really touching statement

00:03:12.601 --> 00:03:14.300
about his retirement.
He said...

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:19.234
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.234 --> 00:03:21.067
Some more TV news --
the new season

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:22.868
of "The Bachelor" is underway.

00:03:22.868 --> 00:03:24.968
But some people are complaining
that this year's Bachelor

00:03:24.968 --> 00:03:27.000
is too boring.
-Yeah.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:28.534
-Yeah.
You think so?

00:03:28.534 --> 00:03:31.033
Well, the producers have decided
to do something about it.

00:03:31.033 --> 00:03:32.200
Watch this.

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:33.334
-The word is out.

00:03:33.334 --> 00:03:35.667
This year's Bachelor
is just too boring.

00:03:35.667 --> 00:03:37.934
America, we heard you
loud and clear.

00:03:37.934 --> 00:03:40.667
So we sent Zach home,
and we're replacing him with...

00:03:40.667 --> 00:03:42.901
-Tom [bleep] Brady!

00:03:42.901 --> 00:03:44.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:44.734 --> 00:03:47.234
Look out, Bachelor nation,
'cause Tom B.

00:03:47.234 --> 00:03:49.033
is on a permanent vacation!

00:03:49.033 --> 00:03:52.100
This retiree is ready to party!
[ Air horn blares ]

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:54.868
He's DTF --
done throwing footballs!

00:03:54.868 --> 00:03:56.667
And he wants one more ring!

00:03:56.667 --> 00:03:58.801
I'm talking Neil Lane bling!

00:03:58.801 --> 00:04:00.667
So, huddle up
in the Fantasy Suite

00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:02.501
and get ready
to touchdown there!

00:04:02.501 --> 00:04:03.968
Hut, hut, what?!

00:04:03.968 --> 00:04:06.133
"The Bachelor" --
fall in love with the GOAT!

00:04:06.133 --> 00:04:08.367
-[ Screaming ]

00:04:08.367 --> 00:04:09.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:09.667 --> 00:04:10.767
-Exciting.

00:04:10.767 --> 00:04:12.167
That's not boring at all.

00:04:12.167 --> 00:04:13.300
-That's exciting!

00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:14.667
-That's what we want to see
right there!

00:04:14.667 --> 00:04:18.100
That's good TV.

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:21.067
Some business news --
today, the C.E.O. of Peloton

00:04:21.067 --> 00:04:23.367
said that the company
will start making money again

00:04:23.367 --> 00:04:26.634
and is no longer
on the "brink of extinction."

00:04:26.634 --> 00:04:28.434
[ Laughter ]

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:30.334
Brink of extinction?

00:04:30.334 --> 00:04:32.167
Calm down.
You're a bike with an iPad.

00:04:32.167 --> 00:04:34.400
[ Laughter ]

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:35.701
Yep, Peloton's C.E.O.

00:04:35.701 --> 00:04:37.868
thinks they'll start
making money in June.

00:04:37.868 --> 00:04:39.100
Everyone's like, "That's great.

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:40.834
Wait. Is there gonna be
another pandemic in June?

00:04:40.834 --> 00:04:43.167
What do you know that we --"
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.167 --> 00:04:45.200
You guys hear about this?
For nearly a week,

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:46.801
crews in Australia
have been searching

00:04:46.801 --> 00:04:49.901
for a radioactive capsule
smaller than a penny

00:04:49.901 --> 00:04:51.100
that fell off a truck,

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:54.300
and today, they finally found it
on a remote road.

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:55.634
[ Cheering ]
Yeah.

00:04:55.634 --> 00:04:57.868
Well, now it's a remote road.
It used to be a city.

00:04:57.868 --> 00:05:03.300
[ Laughter ]

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:05.300
It's actually where Tom Brady
shot that retirement video.

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:07.267
-Really?
[ Laughter ]

00:05:07.267 --> 00:05:08.968
Well, listen to this --
apparently, due to a shrinking

00:05:08.968 --> 00:05:11.701
U.S. cattle herd,
cheeseburgers and steaks

00:05:11.701 --> 00:05:14.267
are about to get more expensive.

00:05:14.267 --> 00:05:16.901
And now Americans are looking
for other types of meat.

00:05:16.901 --> 00:05:17.968
And I don't want to say
it's bad,

00:05:17.968 --> 00:05:20.567
but Punxsutawney Phil
is now "missing."

00:05:20.567 --> 00:05:22.634
[ Laughter ]

00:05:22.634 --> 00:05:25.601
-Oh, no.

00:05:25.601 --> 00:05:27.534
-Hey, I heard about a 6-year-old
in Michigan

00:05:27.534 --> 00:05:29.133
who was playing
on his dad's phone

00:05:29.133 --> 00:05:31.667
and accidentally ordered
a thousand dollars worth

00:05:31.667 --> 00:05:34.267
of food on Grubhub.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:34.267 --> 00:05:36.167
Yeah, he ordered
one cheeseburger.

00:05:36.167 --> 00:05:37.634
-Oh, really?
[ Laughter ]

00:05:37.634 --> 00:05:39.400
-With -- With an egg on it.

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:41.167
[ Laughter ]

00:05:41.167 --> 00:05:43.300
Tomorrow is Groundhog Day,
which, of course, means tonight

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:46.033
is Groundhog Day Eve,
so it's only appropriate

00:05:46.033 --> 00:05:48.968
if I read that classic story
we all know and love.

00:05:48.968 --> 00:05:50.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:50.634 --> 00:05:54.734
♪♪

00:05:54.734 --> 00:05:56.834
'Twas the night
before Groundhog Day,

00:05:56.834 --> 00:05:59.067
and, oh, what a treat-a.

00:05:59.067 --> 00:06:00.634
[ Laughter ]

00:06:00.634 --> 00:06:01.634
-"Treat-a."
-What?

00:06:01.634 --> 00:06:03.167
-"Treat-a."
-"Treat-a."

00:06:03.167 --> 00:06:05.467
-"Treat-a."
-Yep, this is page one.

00:06:05.467 --> 00:06:08.367
-Yep.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:10.534
Oh, what a treat-a.
-Treat-a.

00:06:10.534 --> 00:06:12.634
-Dry January was over.

00:06:12.634 --> 00:06:15.634
So we housed
Skinnygirl margaritas.

00:06:15.634 --> 00:06:18.834
On Fireball, on Jager,
on anything potent.

00:06:18.834 --> 00:06:22.334
We'll get so wrecked,
we'll take advice from a rodent.

00:06:22.334 --> 00:06:25.300
Phil climbs out of his hole
and sees such a crowd.

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:28.067
Then says, "I was sleeping.
Why the hell are you so loud?"

00:06:28.067 --> 00:06:29.400
[ Laughter ]

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:32.067
The people wished for spring,
warmth, and good luck,

00:06:32.067 --> 00:06:35.100
while Phil ignores a FaceTime
from Staten Island Chuck.

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:36.968
[ Laughter ]

00:06:36.968 --> 00:06:40.000
Men in top hats gather round
as their future is read

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:43.067
while Phil prays Bill de Blasio
doesn't drop him on his head.

00:06:43.067 --> 00:06:47.200
[ Laughter ]

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:50.601
The men watched Phil closely.
What news has he brought?

00:06:50.601 --> 00:06:53.033
After they touch him,
they'll need rabies shots.

00:06:53.033 --> 00:06:54.300
[ Laughter ]

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:57.400
If Phil sees no shadow,
soon we'll have spring.

00:06:57.400 --> 00:07:00.767
They lift him up
like a fat hamster "Lion King."

00:07:00.767 --> 00:07:03.601
They look at the ground,
"Is it light, is it shady?"

00:07:03.601 --> 00:07:07.701
while Phil's thinking, "Man,
I gotta retire like Brady."

00:07:07.701 --> 00:07:10.501
Shadow or not,
the townspeople cheer.

00:07:10.501 --> 00:07:13.734
Merry Groundhog Day to all.
Now pass me a beer.

00:07:13.734 --> 00:07:15.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:17.601
We have a great show.
Give it up for The Roots,

00:07:17.601 --> 00:07:19.167
ladies and gentlemen,
right there!

00:07:19.167 --> 00:07:20.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:20.801 --> 00:07:22.334
-♪ 21 pounds ♪

00:07:22.334 --> 00:07:23.801
♪ Let's get down, y'all ♪

00:07:23.801 --> 00:07:26.901
♪ Hey, hey, hey, hey ♪

00:07:26.901 --> 00:07:29.334
-What a show!
Thank you very much.

00:07:29.334 --> 00:07:31.334
What a show
we have for you tonight.

00:07:31.334 --> 00:07:34.934
He is a five-time
World Series champion

00:07:34.934 --> 00:07:37.901
and a member of the baseball
Hall of Fame.

00:07:37.901 --> 00:07:42.033
New York Yankee legend
Derek Jeter is here tonight!

00:07:42.033 --> 00:07:43.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:43.367 --> 00:07:44.734
-The man!
-The best.

00:07:44.734 --> 00:07:46.334
-The best!
-Jetes!

00:07:46.334 --> 00:07:47.901
-Jeter!

00:07:47.901 --> 00:07:49.667
-My favorite.
-Lovely.

00:07:49.667 --> 00:07:51.767
-Yeah, I was so lucky to see

00:07:51.767 --> 00:07:55.300
most of his important,
big milestone games.

00:07:55.300 --> 00:07:57.367
I used to go to the games all
the time with Lorne Michaels,

00:07:57.367 --> 00:08:00.534
and we used to sit there.
And I'm behind --

00:08:00.534 --> 00:08:01.934
You know, sometimes,
we'd end up on camera,

00:08:01.934 --> 00:08:04.701
'cause the seats are right
behind home plate.

00:08:04.701 --> 00:08:07.834
But I just never knew kind of
what to do with my hands.

00:08:07.834 --> 00:08:08.901
So I would just
kind of get nervous.

00:08:08.901 --> 00:08:10.701
And I'd be like,
"Come on, Derek."

00:08:10.701 --> 00:08:12.567
I was rooting for him
all the time.

00:08:12.567 --> 00:08:15.033
So, every time you watch these
highlight videos of Derek,

00:08:15.033 --> 00:08:17.501
you could see one nerd
in the background going...

00:08:17.501 --> 00:08:19.667
[ Laughter ]

00:08:19.667 --> 00:08:21.434
-Waah!
-And, yeah, that's me, yeah.

00:08:21.434 --> 00:08:22.934
But anyways,
Derek Jeter is here tonight.

00:08:22.934 --> 00:08:24.701
I love that guy.
-The best.

00:08:24.701 --> 00:08:26.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:26.200 --> 00:08:29.167
-Speaking of love,
I love her new single.

00:08:29.167 --> 00:08:30.901
It's called "You Only Love Me."

00:08:30.901 --> 00:08:32.200
It is out right now.

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:34.868
And she stars in season two
of the animated series

00:08:34.868 --> 00:08:36.901
"Kung Fu Panda:
The Dragon Knight,"

00:08:36.901 --> 00:08:38.434
which is streaming now
on Netflix.

00:08:38.434 --> 00:08:40.467
Rita Ora is here!
-Wow!

00:08:40.467 --> 00:08:43.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:43.067 --> 00:08:45.534
We're gonna talk to Rita Ora,
then she's performing

00:08:45.534 --> 00:08:47.934
"You Only Love Me"
later in the show.

00:08:47.934 --> 00:08:49.567
Rita Ora in the house.
Come on.

00:08:49.567 --> 00:08:52.634
[ Cheers and applause ]
The best.

00:08:52.634 --> 00:08:54.901
Hey, guys, it is time
for our latest installment

00:08:54.901 --> 00:08:57.133
of "Tonight Show Polls."
Here we go.

00:08:57.133 --> 00:09:01.667
-♪ Tonight Show Polls ♪

00:09:01.667 --> 00:09:03.701
-These are polls.
Polls are very popular.

00:09:03.701 --> 00:09:05.501
-True, people love them.
-Yeah, people love them.

00:09:05.501 --> 00:09:06.934
Adults love them,
kids love them.

00:09:06.934 --> 00:09:09.000
-Everybody loves them --
grandpa, grandma.

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:10.868
-Grandpa loves them?
-No.

00:09:10.868 --> 00:09:12.000
-No.
-He doesn't like them.

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:13.200
-Yeah.
-He likes the poles more

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:15.334
at the strip club.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:15.334 --> 00:09:16.501
-I wish -- I --

00:09:16.501 --> 00:09:19.200
[ Laughter ]

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:21.300
I wish my grandma liked polls.

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:23.200
-Why?
What's the matter?

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:24.234
-Huh?

00:09:24.234 --> 00:09:27.000
-Why doesn't your grandma
like polls?

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:28.601
She loves polls.
Every time I --

00:09:28.601 --> 00:09:30.334
Every time I go
to your grandma's house,

00:09:30.334 --> 00:09:33.067
it's like she goes --
she would read polls to me.

00:09:33.067 --> 00:09:34.734
-Sorry.
I hate to interrupt you.

00:09:34.734 --> 00:09:36.868
You didn't hear what happened?
-No.

00:09:36.868 --> 00:09:39.367
-Last -- Last Christmas.

00:09:39.367 --> 00:09:41.267
-Right.
-We're out at the house...

00:09:41.267 --> 00:09:42.868
-Yeah.
-...having some eggnog,

00:09:42.868 --> 00:09:44.200
stuff like that.

00:09:44.200 --> 00:09:46.400
I think she was probably is
medicated or something.

00:09:46.400 --> 00:09:48.200
-Well, she has a lot of meds,
sure, yeah.

00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:50.634
-Yeah, but she was wearing her
wig and everything, it was cute,

00:09:50.634 --> 00:09:52.367
to have her over there.
-Oh, she's funny.

00:09:52.367 --> 00:09:53.801
-Never mind. I don't even
want to talk about it.

00:09:53.801 --> 00:09:54.934
-What happened?
What happened?

00:09:54.934 --> 00:09:56.267
-What?
-What happened?

00:09:56.267 --> 00:09:58.067
-Well, it was Christmas Eve.

00:09:58.067 --> 00:10:01.167
And I don't know,
she was stumbling home.

00:10:01.167 --> 00:10:02.601
-Yeah?

00:10:02.601 --> 00:10:04.367
-And, uh, my grandma
got run over by a reindeer.

00:10:04.367 --> 00:10:06.033
